{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-336411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity $v$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=4{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+9t.$ Calculate the acceleration $a$ of the particle at time $t.$\n\n$a(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-336411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+9t) \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}-4t+9\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-336411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a473f950ca02cb6db7ee132f1b9de240125d4e28540344c2d876322ff93788c7"} {"question" "q-336411" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-336411" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12t^2-4t+9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-102616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity $v$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of a particle at time $t$ (in seconds) is given by $v(t)=(t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+4t).$ Calculate the velocity of the particle when the acceleration $a$ is equal to $6\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-102616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+4t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1+4 \\\\  & =5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=6,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡t & =1 \\\\ {e}^{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)} & ={e}^{1} \\\\ t & =e\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, to calculate the velocity at time $t=e,$ we substitute this into the equation for the velocity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(e) & =(e\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+4e) \\\\  & =e(1)+4e \\\\  & =5e\\text{ m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity when $a=6\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is $5e\\text{ m/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-102616" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a473f950ca02cb6db7ee132f1b9de240125d4e28540344c2d876322ff93788c7"} {"question" "q-102616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-102616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4\\text{ m/s}"] ["math" "4e\\text{ m/s}"] ["math" "5\\text{ m/s}"] ["math" "5e\\text{ m/s}"] ["math" "e\\text{ m/s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-102616" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5e\\text{ m/s}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-315537" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity $v$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of a particle at time $t$ (in seconds) is given by $v(t)=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}.$ Calculate the velocity of the particle when the acceleration $a$ is equal to $\\frac{1}{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nWhen $a=\\frac{1}{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ the velocity is $v=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-315537" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2t+1}{2\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=\\frac{1}{2},$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{2t+1}{2\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{2t+1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}} \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7} & =2t+1 \\\\ {(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7})}^{2} & ={(2t+1)}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{2}+t+7 & =4{t}^{2}+4t+1 \\\\ 0 & =3{t}^{2}+3t-6 \\\\ 0 & ={t}^{2}+t-2 \\\\ 0 & =(t-1)(t+2) \\\\ t & =1,\\,-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $t=1$ since $t\\ge 0.$\n\nThen, to calculate the velocity at time $t=1,$ we substitute this into the equation for the velocity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+1+7} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+7} \\\\  & =3\\text{ m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity when $a=\\frac{1}{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is $v=3\\,\\text{m/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-315537" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a473f950ca02cb6db7ee132f1b9de240125d4e28540344c2d876322ff93788c7"} {"question" "q-315537" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-315537" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-2361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity $v$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of a particle at time $t$ (in seconds) is given by $v(t)=4{t}^{2}-16t+15.$ Calculate the velocity of the particle when the acceleration $a$ is equal to $0\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-2361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}-16t+15) \\\\  & =8t-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=0,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =8t-16 \\\\ 8t & =16 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, to calculate the velocity at time $t=2,$ we substitute this into the equation for the velocity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =4(2)^{2}-16(2)+15 \\\\  & =16-32+15 \\\\  & =-1\\text{ m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity when $a=0\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is $-1\\,\\text{m/s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-2361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a473f950ca02cb6db7ee132f1b9de240125d4e28540344c2d876322ff93788c7"} {"question" "q-2361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-2361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1\\text{ m/s}"] ["math" "-3\\text{ m/s}"] ["math" "1\\text{ m/s}"] ["math" "2\\text{ m/s}"] ["math" "3\\text{ m/s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-2361" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1\\text{ m/s}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-336415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity $v$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=\\frac{3{t}^{2}-5t+2}{t}.$ Calculate the acceleration $a$ of the particle at time $t.$\n\n$a(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-336415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3{t}^{2}-5t+2}{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-5+\\frac{2}{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-5+2{t}^{-1}) \\\\  & =3+2(-{t}^{-2}) \\\\  & =3-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-336415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a473f950ca02cb6db7ee132f1b9de240125d4e28540344c2d876322ff93788c7"} {"question" "q-336415" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-336415" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3-\\frac{2}{t^2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-336441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2},$ where $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the time when the particle's acceleration is equal to $a=70\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nThe acceleration is $70\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ at\n$t=$\n{{field-1}} seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-336441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(12{t}^{2}-2t) \\\\  & =24t-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=70,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}70 & =24t-2 \\\\ 24t & =72 \\\\ t & =3\\text{ }\\text{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration is $70\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ at $t=3$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-336441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a473f950ca02cb6db7ee132f1b9de240125d4e28540344c2d876322ff93788c7"} {"question" "q-336441" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-336441" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-336448" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=5{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2},$ where $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the particle's acceleration at $t=1$ second.\n\n$a(1)=$\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-336448" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =15{t}^{2}-4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(15{t}^{2}-4t) \\\\  & =30t-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=1$ second, we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =30(1)-4 \\\\  & =26\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-336448" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a473f950ca02cb6db7ee132f1b9de240125d4e28540344c2d876322ff93788c7"} {"question" "q-336448" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-336448" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "26"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-2359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=4{t}^{3}+10{t}^{2}-15$, where $t$ is measured in seconds.  Find the particle's acceleration at $t=3$ seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-2359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}+10{t}^{2}-15) \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}+20t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(12{t}^{2}+20t) \\\\  & =24t+20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=3$, we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(3) & =24(3)+20 \\\\  & =72+20 \\\\  & =92\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration when $t=3$ seconds is $92\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-2359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a473f950ca02cb6db7ee132f1b9de240125d4e28540344c2d876322ff93788c7"} {"question" "q-2359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951961/state.json" "file_sha256" "2c49b9a56c321999a18632d281dd633429eee145ba4bbc2f3993a28f77ec6916"} {"question" "q-2359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "100\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "72\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "88\